# Change

`ciel_runtime.py` imports `runtime_input_delivery_health` and binds the existing
`TuiObservationHttpPorts.delivery_health` callback to the shared
`_RUNTIME_INPUT_STATUS_REPOSITORY`. The adapter and port architecture are unchanged.
Chat and receiver observations already resolve that same repository via their bound
callbacks.

# Regression

`tests/test_tui_observation.py::TuiObservationRouterIntegrationTests::test_production_factory_binds_shared_delivery_health_over_http`
exercises the production factory and JSON writer through temporary loopback HTTP.
Both `/ca/tui/status` and `/ca/tui/health` are tested against complete and corrupt
private history. The test asserts the exact callback repository, two queued inputs,
coverage, age, corrupt physical line, payload exclusion, no claimed launcher hold,
and byte-for-byte unchanged fixture histories.

Before the factory fix, both fixture cases failed with `Actual: not called`.
After the fix, the focused regression passed. The TUI observation and delivery-health
files passed together: 20 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors (3.322 seconds).
`py_compile` and focused `git diff --check` passed.

# Isolation

Tests ran in a subprocess after removing inherited `CIEL_RUNTIME_*`, provider/session
environment, and token/secret/password/credential/API-key environment. The supported
`isolate_runtime_state()` helper supplied temporary config and an ephemeral port;
state/workspace paths and launch cwd were set to that temporary directory. HTTP
fixtures bound loopback port 0 and closed their own servers. No live runtime actions,
commits, pushes, deployments, or changes to the worker-owned router HTTP/retry files.
